## 2. PostgreSQL database design

Use Flyway migrations, following your existing migration numbering convention.

### V101 — Stock instruments

```sql
CREATE TABLE stock_instruments (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    company_name VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL,
    canonical_symbol VARCHAR(30) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    exchange VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL,
    yahoo_symbol VARCHAR(50),
    listing_date DATE,
    active BOOLEAN DEFAULT TRUE,
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE TABLE instrument_symbol_history (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    instrument_id BIGINT REFERENCES stock_instruments(id),
    yahoo_symbol VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
    valid_from DATE NOT NULL,
    valid_to DATE,
    UNIQUE(instrument_id, valid_from)
);
```

### V102 — Historical prices

```sql
CREATE TABLE historical_prices (
    id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    instrument_id BIGINT NOT NULL
        REFERENCES stock_instruments(id),

    trading_date DATE NOT NULL,

    open_price NUMERIC(18,6),
    high_price NUMERIC(18,6),
    low_price NUMERIC(18,6),
    close_price NUMERIC(18,6),
